WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.320
[upbeat music]

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.580
Welcome. In this module,

3
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:09.680
we'll explore how chiplet technology
provides a yield advantage,

4
00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:15.370
a design cost advantage, and accelerates
time to market, all of which

5
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:20.160
contribute to a more cost-effective
and scalable semiconductor industry.

6
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.500
Let's start with yield advantage.

7
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:27.760
In traditional monolithic chip
designs, larger dies have lower yields

8
00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.780
because any defect in the wafer
could result in a faulty chip.

9
00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:35.560
But with chiplets,
the die sizes are smaller,

10
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.260
which increases the number of functional
dies per wafer and improves yield.

11
00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.800
This leads to lower overall
manufacturing costs.

12
00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.640
Next, we have the design cost advantage.

13
00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:50.920
Advanced semiconductor
nodes are expensive,

14
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:56.100
and not all components of a system benefit
equally from cutting-edge technology.

15
00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:01.380
Chiplets allow manufacturers to use
the optimal process for each function.

16
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:06.400
For example, logic can be
fabricated at the latest nodes,

17
00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:12.040
while analog and memory functions remain
in older, more cost-effective nodes.

18
00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:16.900
This leads us to another key
benefit, faster time to market.

19
00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:21.070
By reusing pre-designed
chiplets, companies can reduce

20
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:25.900
development time and avoid the risks
of designing an entire chip from scratch.

21
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:30.540
Whether using in-house chiplets
or those from third parties,

22
00:01:30.780 --> 00:01:34.980
such as from the marketplace
in OCP's, Open Chiplet Economy,

23
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:39.700
businesses can accelerate product
launches and gain a competitive edge.

24
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:43.060
Of course, these benefits
come with some trade-offs.

25
00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:46.520
While chiplet architectures
reduce die costs,

26
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.840
they can increase packaging
and testing costs.

27
00:01:50.360 --> 00:01:54.580
However, the overall balance
still favors cost savings,

28
00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:00.100
especially in scenarios where chiplets
enable customization and scalability.

29
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:05.720
The chiplet model is revolutionizing
semiconductor economics.

30
00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:09.720
Whether it's better yield,
optimized design costs,

31
00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:14.400
or a faster time to market,
the financial benefits are clear.

32
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.100
Continue exploring this module to dive
deeper into chiplet cost trends,

33
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.660
estimating costs,
and the open chiplet economy.

34
00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:28.760
[upbeat music]

